WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.829 --> 00:00:16.394
The tree soon had a new pair of visitors: Demi and Dan, who'd been collecting leaves.

2
00:00:17.814 --> 00:00:21.616
"Let's sort our leaves," Demi said, climbing into the tree.

3
00:00:25.077 --> 00:00:27.919
Dan held up two different leaves and sighed.

4
00:00:27.939 --> 00:00:33.081
"If only I had a microscope, I could show you some interesting things."

5
00:00:34.782 --> 00:00:39.904
"You'll soon—um Demi caught himself before he revealed the secret.

6
00:00:39.924 --> 00:00:43.025
"Uh look over there!"

7
00:00:45.946 --> 00:00:50.308
Jo was reading a book as she walked along with Teddy trotting behind her.

8
00:00:50.328 --> 00:00:56.031
"I wonder how long before they notice us," Dan whispered.

9
00:00:57.071 --> 00:01:01.209
Both boys sat completely still as Jo and Teddy approached.

10
00:01:02.670 --> 00:01:09.073
Jo was so absorbed in her book—which she'd been trying to read all week—that she almost wandered into

11
00:01:09.093 --> 00:01:09.513
the brook.

12
00:01:10.534 --> 00:01:14.276
Fortunately Teddy interrupted her reading in the nick of time.

13
00:01:14.296 --> 00:01:17.938
"Mama, I want to fish!"

14
00:01:18.378 --> 00:01:21.000
Teddy said, tugging on his mother's sleeve.

15
00:01:22.180 --> 00:01:25.022
"You'll need a fishing pole," Jo replied.

16
00:01:26.403 --> 00:01:31.001
Before she could look for a suitable stick, a willow bough fell at her feet.

17
00:01:32.722 --> 00:01:36.945
Looking up, she saw the boys laughing in their secret hideaway.

18
00:01:36.965 --> 00:01:40.266
"I want to climb up there!"

19
00:01:40.727 --> 00:01:41.427
Teddy said.

20
00:01:41.447 --> 00:01:46.430
"I'll come down, and then you can come up," Demi said.

21
00:01:46.450 --> 00:01:49.492
"I need to find Daisy anyway."

22
00:01:52.173 --> 00:01:56.716
Leaning down, Dan scooped up Teddy and then offered Jo his hand.

23
00:01:58.188 --> 00:02:00.089
"There's plenty of room for you too, Mrs.

24
00:02:00.149 --> 00:02:06.354
Bauer." A moment later Jo was enjoying a shady seat.

25
00:02:08.035 --> 00:02:13.719
"I haven't climbed a tree since I was married," she said, looking pleased with herself.

26
00:02:15.260 --> 00:02:18.522
"When I was a girl, I was quite fond of climbing trees."

27
00:02:18.542 --> 00:02:25.947
"Now you can read if you want, and I'll take care of Teddy," Dan said, pulling some string

28
00:02:26.007 --> 00:02:29.437
and a pin from his pocket so he could make a fishing rod.

29
00:02:30.977 --> 00:02:32.838
"What were you and Demi doing up here?"

30
00:02:33.258 --> 00:02:33.978
Jo asked.

31
00:02:33.998 --> 00:02:37.839
"Just talking about the leaves we found."

32
00:02:38.959 --> 00:02:43.281
Dan bent the pin into a hook and handed the fishing rod to Teddy.

33
00:02:44.601 --> 00:02:49.622
He wrapped an arm protectively around Teddy, so the little boy wouldn't fall.

34
00:02:49.642 --> 00:02:54.824
"I'm glad you're taking the time to talk to Demi," Jo said.

35
00:02:56.116 --> 00:02:58.617
"He thinks you're the bravest boy in the world."

36
00:02:58.637 --> 00:03:03.519
"I didn't know if you'd trust me with him," Dan replied.

37
00:03:05.160 --> 00:03:06.160
Jo looked puzzled.

38
00:03:06.180 --> 00:03:07.761
"Why not?"

39
00:03:08.181 --> 00:03:08.761
she asked.

40
00:03:08.781 --> 00:03:13.964
"Well, Demi is so kind and good Dan began.

41
00:03:13.984 --> 00:03:18.506
"Yes, he's just like his father, John."

42
00:03:18.526 --> 00:03:26.590
"I thought you'd want him to stay away from me because I can be a bad influence," Dan

43
00:03:26.650 --> 00:03:27.170
went on.

44
00:03:27.190 --> 00:03:30.613
"You're not a bad influence!"

45
00:03:31.073 --> 00:03:37.918
Jo said loudly, "and I do trust—" "Shh, Mama, you'll scare the fish!"

46
00:03:38.379 --> 00:03:39.380
Teddy interrupted.

47
00:03:40.961 --> 00:03:43.162
Jo continued in a hushed voice.

48
00:03:43.182 --> 00:03:46.325
"I do trust you, Dan.

49
00:03:47.266 --> 00:03:50.168
Not only with Demi, but with my own sons.

50
00:03:51.372 --> 00:03:56.616
You've tried to improve your behavior every week, and there are some things you can teach better than

51
00:03:56.937 --> 00:03:57.457
any of us."

52
00:03:57.477 --> 00:03:59.579
"I can?"

53
00:03:59.959 --> 00:04:01.661
Dan said in amazement.

54
00:04:01.681 --> 00:04:08.967
"Yes, you've had to make your way in the real world, so you can teach Demi some common

55
00:04:09.047 --> 00:04:16.112
sense. That's something he can't get from books, no matter how many stories he reads.

56
00:04:17.253 --> 00:04:20.136
Meanwhile he can improve your sense of right and wrong."

57
00:04:22.020 --> 00:04:26.141
Words could not express how pleased Dan was by Jo's praise.

58
00:04:27.822 --> 00:04:32.043
No one had ever trusted him or taken the time to discover the good in him.

59
00:04:33.443 --> 00:04:38.685
He felt he had friends now and a place in the world, as well as something to live

60
00:04:38.745 --> 00:04:43.046
for. "Thank you, ma'am" was all he could say.

61
00:04:44.567 --> 00:04:48.828
Suddenly Teddy shouted, "A fish—I caught a fish!"

62
00:04:51.324 --> 00:04:56.466
Dan helped Teddy pull in his catch and then asked, "Do you know what kind of fish this

63
00:04:56.606 --> 00:04:58.047
is? A trout!

64
00:04:58.547 --> 00:05:02.308
I've never even seen one here before—good job!"

65
00:05:04.189 --> 00:05:09.611
The three of them went back to the house to show off Teddy's fine catch before Asia cooked

66
00:05:09.651 --> 00:05:10.292
it for supper.

67
00:05:14.693 --> 00:05:18.155
For a few hours, the seat in the willow tree remained empty.

68
00:05:19.875 --> 00:05:25.823
But around sunset a boy sneaked up the drive, across the lawn, and into the tree.

69
00:05:27.665 --> 00:05:31.107
Jack was trying to decide what to do next when Mr.

70
00:05:31.167 --> 00:05:33.549
Bauer appeared below on his evening walk.

71
00:05:34.830 --> 00:05:37.391
Jack took a deep breath and called out to him.

72
00:05:37.411 --> 00:05:38.472
"Hi, Mr.

73
00:05:38.532 --> 00:05:45.217
Bauer." "I'm glad to see you, Jack," the professor said, looking up.

74
00:05:46.538 --> 00:05:52.194
"I didn't want to come back," Jack blurted out, "but my uncle made me because this school is

75
00:05:52.234 --> 00:05:53.495
the cheapest one around.

76
00:05:55.296 --> 00:05:56.798
He punished me pretty hard."

77
00:05:57.839 --> 00:05:59.960
Jack kicked nervously at the tree trunk.

78
00:05:59.980 --> 00:06:02.723
"Are you going to punish me, Mr.

79
00:06:02.763 --> 00:06:05.265
Bauer? Is everyone still mad at me?"

80
00:06:05.285 --> 00:06:09.589
"I can't predict how the boys will react.

81
00:06:10.529 --> 00:06:16.915
But since Dan and Nat suffered so much punishment without doing anything wrong, you should probably suffer some

82
00:06:16.995 --> 00:06:18.156
consequences too."

83
00:06:19.876 --> 00:06:24.120
"I returned Tommy's dollar, and I said I was sorry in my note to you.

84
00:06:24.621 --> 00:06:25.441
Isn't that enough?"

85
00:06:25.461 --> 00:06:32.287
"No, you should apologize to the three boys," the professor said.

86
00:06:33.729 --> 00:06:35.671
Jack didn't feel brave enough for that.

87
00:06:35.691 --> 00:06:40.155
"What if I auction off some of my things?"

88
00:06:40.635 --> 00:06:41.196
he asked.

89
00:06:42.437 --> 00:06:45.820
The professor understood how much money meant to Jack.

90
00:06:47.376 --> 00:06:51.439
"First, it would be better to give away your things than to make money from them.

91
00:06:52.780 --> 00:06:57.023
Second, your friends would value your apology more than your things.

92
00:06:58.724 --> 00:07:03.127
You should think about what's more important to you—money or friends."

93
00:07:05.249 --> 00:07:08.131
Jack watched the willow branches sway in the breeze.

94
00:07:08.151 --> 00:07:12.854
"Okay, fine," he muttered.

95
00:07:12.874 --> 00:07:15.096
"I'll apologize."

96
00:07:16.968 --> 00:07:23.574
So Jack climbed down from the tree, and, with the professor's help, he took his first steps back

97
00:07:23.654 --> 00:07:25.276
into the Plumfield family.
